    "Scouting Notes": "Very interesting setup. Reminds me a bit of lefty Tony Batista or Aristides Aquino.\n Very open, almost facing the pitcher, but gets closed off and has not seemed to have any trouble with timing so far.\n Really good bat to ball skills, should be a pretty low K type of guy.\n Seems to have pretty good plate discipline early on.\n Not sure on the power, is said to have some raw pop, but haven't seen it much in games yet.\n People think he will likely have to move off of catcher to first, and given his passed ball issues early on, that seems believable.\n His value would be much higher at catcher, but if he can't handle it then they can't force it.\n The bat is very interesting, will be one to follow. Aggressive assignment to A+ (likely partially due to injury), but handling well early on.",
